// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.2 - THE TWO ATTACHMENTS THE PACK-A-PUNCHED WEAPONS CRASHED WITHOUT
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Firing a Pack-a-Punched ported weapon froze the game hard - no GSC error,
//  the console log simply ended mid-line. The upgraded defs are the only half
//  of each pair that carries an `attachments` field, which is why the base
//  weapon fired fine and only the upgraded one died.
//
//  Of the 8 attachments those defs name, six were already in mod.ff as
//  dependencies. These two were not:
//      holo            <- qbb95_upgraded_zm
//      steadyaim_smg   <- vector_upgraded_zm, vector_extclip_upgraded_zm
//  steadyaim_smg is the Vector's, which is the weapon the user froze on.
//
//  🛑 ,defaultattachment IS NOT MISSING and must not be added here - it is
//  already declared at mod_base.zone:476. Its real asset name carries a LEADING
//  COMMA (the Unlinker prints it as `attachment, ,defaultattachment`), so a
//  naive lookup for "defaultattachment" reports a false absence. That false
//  positive cost one wrong diagnosis; check the raw listing, not a built key.
// ============================================================================
attachment,holo
attachment,steadyaim_smg

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.3 - THE PACK-A-PUNCH ATTACHMENT TABLE, UNDER A MOD-PRIVATE NAME
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  _zm_weapons::add_attachments() looks the UPGRADED weapon name up in
//  `zm/pap_attach.csv` and assigns level.zombie_weapons[w].default_attachment
//  from column 1. Every stock Pack-a-Punched weapon has a row there; none of
//  the nine ported ones did - so a packed weapon was built with an attachment
//  set its def requires and nothing supplied. That is the crash on firing.
//
//  🛑 THE STOCK TABLE CANNOT BE OVERRIDDEN. `zm/pap_attach.csv` is owned by
//  patch_zm.ff; declaring that exact name here makes mod.ff the owner, mod.ff
//  loads first, and the owning zone then dies with
//      COM_ERROR Attempting to override asset ... from zone 'mod'
//  which is the same shape that made Origins unbootable in v1.19.0.
//
//  🌟 SO IT SHIPS UNDER A NEW NAME AND IS SELECTED IN SCRIPT.
//  _zm_weapons.gsc:582 reads `if ( isdefined( level.weapon_attachment_table ) )
//  table = level.weapon_attachment_table;` - a hook Treyarch left open. The
//  file carries ALL 29 stock rows verbatim plus 7 of ours, so pointing the
//  whole game at it changes nothing for any stock weapon.
// ============================================================================
stringtable,zm/pap_attach_qol.csv

// ============================================================================
//  v2.14.16 - SUBTITLES: one table per map, alias -> explicit text, clean text.
//  Built by `zm_qol - dev\subtitles\build_tables.py` from Whisper large-v3
//  transcripts of the 10,722 character clips; read by tablelookup() in
//  scripts/zm/zmqol_subtitles.gsc. Text only - no stock asset is touched.
// ============================================================================
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_transit.csv
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_highrise.csv
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_buried.csv
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_nuked.csv
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_prison.csv
stringtable,zm/zmqol_subs_zm_tomb.csv

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.5 - THE 13 ATTACHMENTUNIQUES, AS FASTFILE ASSETS THIS TIME
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  🛑 THE ACTUAL CAUSE OF THE PACK-A-PUNCH CRASH, MEASURED IN THE RUNTIME LOG.
//  console_zm.log prints, once per weapon, at map load:
//      Couldn't find attachmentunique 'au_mp7_dualclip'
//      Couldn't find attachmentunique 'au_mp7_none'
//      ... 13 lines, EXACTLY the 13 the nine upgraded defs name, and ZERO
//      lines for any of the 89 stock au_* the mod already ships.
//  The upgraded def is the only half of each pair with an `attachmentUniques`
//  field, so a Pack-a-Punched weapon is built pointing at a record that does
//  not exist, and the first shot dereferences it: 0xC0000005.
//
//  🛑 WHY v1.89.1 DID NOT FIX THIS. It put all 13 in the raw `attachmentunique\`
//  folder and confirmed them inside the deployed mod.iwd - both true, and
//  irrelevant. RAW IS NOT THE DELIVERY PATH FOR THIS ASSET TYPE. All 13 are
//  verified present in the deployed mod.iwd and the engine still cannot find
//  them. The 89 that work are FASTFILE assets: mod_base.zone declares 91
//  `attachmentunique,` lines and mod_locations.zone declared none. The raw
//  folder is what the Linker was fed from, not what the game reads.
//
//  Resolvable with no new --load: all 13 are in common_mp.ff, and the three
//  peacekeeper ones in common_patch_mp.ff - both already loaded, last, for the
//  weapon port. No zombies fastfile owns any of these names (checked against
//  common_zm, patch_zm, zm_transit, zm_tomb, zm_buried: 0 matches), so mod.ff
//  owning them cannot re-own anything.
// ============================================================================
attachmentunique,au_mp7_none
attachmentunique,au_mp7_dualclip
attachmentunique,au_vector_none
attachmentunique,au_vector_steadyaim
attachmentunique,au_sig556_none
attachmentunique,au_sig556_gl
attachmentunique,au_sa58_none
attachmentunique,au_sa58_sf
attachmentunique,au_qbb95_none
attachmentunique,au_qbb95_holo
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_none
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_grip
attachmentunique,au_peacekeeper_reflex

// ============================================================================
//  v1.89.6 - THE TWO ALT-WEAPON POINTERS, REPOINTED AT THE ZOMBIES DEFS
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  Declaring the 13 above made the engine finally READ them, and the first boot
//  that did so printed two brand-new lines that had never appeared before:
//      Could not load weapon "gl_sig556_mp"
//      Could not load weapon "sf_sa58_mp"
//  Only 2 of the 13 carry a non-empty `altWeapon`, and both name MULTIPLAYER's
//  weapon - so the packed SIG556's grenade launcher and the packed SA58's
//  select-fire pointed at nothing. `gl_sig556_upgraded_zm` and
//  `sf_sa58_upgraded_zm` were shipped as raw defs in v1.88.0, are confirmed
//  "Loaded weapon:" in the log, and are include_weapon'd on BOTH halves
//  (quality_of_life.gsc:5648-5649, zm_expanded.csc:117-118). Nothing referenced
//  them. BO2-Reimagined edits exactly these two fields and nothing else that
//  matters - independent confirmation of both the defect and the target names.
//
//  🌟 HOW AN ASSET WE DO NOT OWN THE SOURCE FOR GETS EDITED. The Linker resolves
//  a declared asset from the ASSET SEARCH PATH FIRST and only then falls back to
//  a --load'ed fastfile - the same mechanism build_ff.bat already relies on to
//  stage .csc files over the donor's stale copies. So the two edited files sit
//  in `zone_assets\attachmentunique\` and the Linker takes those instead of
//  common_mp.ff's. Verified by dumping the built mod.ff back out with
//  `Unlinker --include-assets attachmentunique`, not by trusting the source file.
//
//  📝 The other 11 are NOT staged and must not be. Reimagined also fills in ~40
//  anim fields per file that MP leaves empty; the user's packed Vector fired and
//  rendered correctly with all 34 of them empty, which proves empty fields
//  inherit from the weapon def. Copying them would be change without cause.
//  Every `camo` the 13 name (camo_mp7, camo_vector, camo_sig556, camo_sa58,
//  camo_qbb, camo_holo, camo_peacekeeper, camo_reflex) is confirmed present in
//  mod.ff, so those fields are correct as extracted too.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
//  v2.9.26 - THE EZZ ANIMATED PACK-A-PUNCH CAMO (user, 2026-09-01: "use the
//  animated pap camos from the ezz mod and replace the current galaxy one").
//
//  Measured out of the installed zm_ezz3.0 (mods folder), not assumed:
//    - EZZ never touches scripts or the PaP index; their per-weapon camo
//      tables keep stock slot 8 = mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2.
//    - Their signature pink/cherry/galaxy animated camo is the material
//      mtl_weapon_camo_mystic (v3.0 contents): the SAME animated techniqueset
//      as dlc2 (mc_sw4_3d_weapon_camo_anim_glow_930950j2), with
//      camo_stellar_ember driving BOTH the Ember and Heat_Map roles,
//      camo_goldgrid_nml as detail/reveal/color/spec, and much hotter
//      constants (intensity 17.5/17.5, flicker 1.6/1.6 vs stock 5.5/11,
//      0.53/0.98). Verified by decoding camo_stellar_ember to PNG and
//      looking at it: pink/red/purple nebula with stars.
//
//  This mod already owns the whole animated dlc2 family (plain + _1/_2/_3,
//  byte-identical texture tables and constants, measured), and every camo
//  table's slot 8 points there - so stamping EZZ's mystic contents onto all
//  four names (zone_assets\materials\mc\, raw JSON beats the --loads) swaps
//  the look everywhere at once, replacing the old MOTD Galaxy image-pixel
//  retexture. The galaxy-pack pixels in camo_zmb_dlc2_ember/_heat/_reveal are
//  no longer referenced by these materials but the image assets stay owned -
//  un-owning a still-declared name is the ERROR_CATALOGUE 35 crash class.
//  The _alt family (static etched camo, different techniqueset) is untouched.
//
//  The two images below are new names; their headers build from the raw
//  .iwi in zone_assets\images\ (EZZ's own files, verbatim bytes) and
//  build.bat's step [1/6] copies the pixels into images\ for mod.iwd.
// ============================================================================

// ============================================================================
//  ADDED SURVIVAL LOCATIONS (2026-09-02 restoration, user request)
//  Power Station (TranZit), Shopping Mall + Dragon Rooftop + Sweatshop (Die
//  Rise), Cell Block (Mob), Borough (Buried), and as of v2.14.0 The Crazy Place
//  (Origins). Everything below was in the pre-strip zone (git d722590) except
//  the XANIM section, which is new - and is the suspected fix for the pre-strip
//  Borough frozen-zombie failure. Cornfield, Maze, Docks and Origins' other
//  three arenas stay out.
//
//  TUNNEL'S TWO MATERIALS WERE REMOVED IN v2.14.0 with the location and PUT
//  BACK IN v2.14.30 (2026-09-08, user: "add back tunnel survival"). Both
//  point at stock art (menu_zm_transit_zclassic_transit /
//  loadscreen_transit_classic) supplied by the --load'ed retail zones.
// ============================================================================

// --- lobby previews + loading screens for the restored locations.
//     JSON sources in zone_assets\materials\; the images they reference are in
//     zone_assets\images\ (and build.bat syncs them into images\ for mod.iwd).
material,menu_zm_transit_zsurvival_power
material,menu_zm_transit_zsurvival_tunnel
material,menu_zm_highrise_zsurvival_shopping_mall
material,menu_zm_highrise_zsurvival_dragon_rooftop
material,menu_zm_highrise_zsurvival_sweatshop
material,menu_zm_buried_zsurvival_street
material,menu_zm_prison_zsurvival_cellblock
material,loadscreen_zm_transit_zstandard_power
material,loadscreen_zm_transit_zstandard_tunnel
material,loadscreen_zm_highrise_zstandard_shopping_mall
material,loadscreen_zm_highrise_zstandard_dragon_rooftop
material,loadscreen_zm_highrise_zstandard_sweatshop
material,loadscreen_zm_buried_zstandard_street
material,loadscreen_zm_prison_zstandard_cellblock

// --- v2.14.0: THE CRAZY PLACE (Origins survival).
//     Both .json sources already shipped in zone_assets\materials\ from the
//     pre-strip era, so only the two declarations below are new. Neither needs
//     a new image: the menu material points at menu_zm_tomb_zsurvival_tomb and
//     the loadscreen at loadscreen_zombie_le_tombeau_zstandard, and both .iwi
//     are already in zone_assets\images\ (and in images\ for mod.iwd).
material,menu_zm_tomb_zsurvival_crazy_place
material,loadscreen_zm_tomb_zstandard_crazy_place

// ============================================================================
//  SURVIVAL PLAYER CHARACTERS (Die Rise + Borough: the CDC/CIA teams)
