// ============================================================================
//  BURIED ZOMBIE XANIMS - NEW vs the pre-strip build; the suspected frozen-
//  zombie fix.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  The pre-strip Borough boot (2026-08-02/03) spawned zombies that stood
//  frozen with everything else measured correct. The pre-strip zone declared
//  the aitypes, characters and xmodels but not ONE xanim - and, measured
//  2026-09-02 with the Unlinker: zm_buried.ff (base, all gametypes) carries
//  NONE of the 495 zombie locomotion/attack/traverse anims; they exist only in
//  so_zclassic_zm_buried.ff (495) / so_zencounter_zm_buried.ff (480). An AI
//  whose animations are not loaded cannot move. BO2-Reimagined's own
//  zone_source\includes\zm_buried.zone declares 433 xanims for exactly this
//  reason; the list below is the measured gap (classic addon minus base map),
//  which is a superset of Reimagined's.
//
//  MOD.FF LOADS ON EVERY MAP, so shared anim NAMES override other maps'
//  copies. Measured before shipping: of the 495, the copies shared with
//  zm_highrise (247), zm_prison (250), zm_tomb (236) and zm_nuked (261 of 263)
//  are BYTE-IDENTICAL to Buried's. The only two that differ anywhere are
//  ai_zombie_jump_up_154 / ai_zombie_crawl_jump_up_154 on zm_nuked (28,983B vs
//  29,018B and 20,781B vs 20,788B) - Nuketown's two 154-unit jump-up traverses
//  will play Buried's near-identical copy. zm_transit shares zero names (its
//  zombie anims live in its own so_ addons). Accepted, documented residual.
// ============================================================================

xanim,ai_zombie_attack_crawl
