// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.0 - MOD-PRIVATE PACK-A-PUNCH CAMO TABLES (camo_qol_*)
//
//  User, 2026-09-03: "make sure the animated pap camo ... is applied to every
//  weapon once they're papped so long as the animated camo patch option is
//  enabled."
//
//  🌟 THE ONLY LEVER §50 LEFT OPEN, AND THIS IS IT. §50 measured that a map's
//  own copy of a camo asset BEATS mod.ff's, which is why index 44 (slot 8, the
//  animated camo) rendered NOTHING on Green Run, Die Rise and Nuketown: those
//  maps ship FOUR-slot tables and the last zone loaded wins. Its closing line
//  was "give a weapon a camo table no map defines" - and a weapon def names its
//  camo asset in a plain `camo\<name>` field, so that is now done by NAME:
//  every affected gun points at camo_qol_<x>, a name no retail fastfile
//  contains, so mod.ff is the ONLY owner and its 13-slot table always draws.
//
//  🌟 AND THE LINKER *DOES* READ A RAW WEAPON FILE - measured 2026-09-03 and it
//  overturns the standing "weapon: the Linker NEVER reads a raw file" note.
//  A probe zone declaring weapon,ak74u_upgraded_zm with zm_transit.ff --load'ed
//  and a hand-edited def in <asset-search-path>/weapons/ linked the camo the RAW
//  file named, not the fastfile's (OAT's ObjLoading carries WeaponRawLoaderT6,
//  path "weapons/<assetName>"). That is what lets the 35 guns mod.ff already
//  owns be retargeted at all - Plutonium's runtime raw loader refuses a name
//  mod.ff owns (checkpoint 149), so weapons\zm\ was never an option for them.
//
//  The two routes, and why each gun is on the one it is on:
//    35 guns mod.ff already owns -> zone_assets\weapons\<name>, linked in here.
//    13 guns only the maps own   -> weapons\zm\<name> raw in mod.iwd, which is
//                                   PROVEN to beat the map's copy (the Jet Gun,
//                                   v2.9.11) and is refused only for mod.ff's.
//
//  🛑 EVERY TABLE WAS MEASURED BEFORE SHIPPING, not assumed: all 38 carry slot 3
//  (index 39, the static zombies camo - the OFF path) and slot 8 (index 44, the
//  animated one) live, and slot 8's baseMaterial set is a SUPERSET of slot 3's
//  in all 38, so no gun can come out with less camo than it has today. Slot 12
//  (index 48, the Origins OFF path) is live in 37 of 38; the gap is
//  camo_qol_slowgun and the Paralyzer is Buried-only, so index 48 never reaches
//  it. The content is a byte copy of mod.ff's own existing camo_<x>, so nothing
//  new is linked - the base materials and images these name are already owned or
//  referenced by the lines above.
// ============================================================================
camo,camo_qol_870mcs
camo,camo_qol_ak74u
camo,camo_qol_an94
camo,camo_qol_b23r
camo,camo_qol_ballistic_knife_80s
camo,camo_qol_chicom
camo,camo_qol_dsr50
camo,camo_qol_fal
camo,camo_qol_fiveseven
camo,camo_qol_galil
camo,camo_qol_hamr
camo,camo_qol_hk416
camo,camo_qol_judge
camo,camo_qol_kard
camo,camo_qol_lsat
camo,camo_qol_m14
camo,camo_qol_m16
camo,camo_qol_m1911
camo,camo_qol_m32
camo,camo_qol_m82
camo,camo_qol_mc96
camo,camo_qol_mg08
camo,camo_qol_mp5
camo,camo_qol_olympia
camo,camo_qol_pdw57
camo,camo_qol_python
camo,camo_qol_raygun
camo,camo_qol_rnma
camo,camo_qol_rpd
camo,camo_qol_saiga
camo,camo_qol_saritch
camo,camo_qol_slowgun
camo,camo_qol_srm1216
camo,camo_qol_svu
camo,camo_qol_type95
