// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.0 - THE THREE ASSETS THE RETARGETED RAW DEFS NEED ON MAPS THAT LACK
//  THEM. A raw weapons\zm\ def is ONE file for all six maps, so where retail
//  ships two different copies of a gun the single file has to name assets that
//  resolve everywhere. Measured per map with Unlinker --list; only two guns of
//  the thirteen diverge at all once the *_patch zone is layered in front (the
//  patch loads first, at 943 vs the base's 944, so its copy is the live one):
//
//    ray_gun_upgraded_zm - transit/highrise/nuked use t6_wpn_zmb_raygun_view
//      and weapon_usa_ray_gun; buried/prison/tomb use the dedicated UPGRADED
//      models. The def shipped is Buried's verbatim, so those three maps are
//      byte-identical to stock, and the two xmodels are declared here so Green
//      Run, Die Rise and Nuketown can draw them too - their PaP'd Ray Gun now
//      uses Treyarch's own Porter's X2 model instead of the base one with a
//      camo. The pixels need no .iwi here: dlczm1-4.ipak are added at startup
//      on EVERY map (console_zm.log, "Added ipak file: dlczm2" on TranZit).
//
//    m14_upgraded_zm - buried/tomb name menu_mp_weapons_m14 for all three icon
//      fields, the other four name hud_icon_m14. The def shipped is TranZit's
//      (hud_icon_m14, four maps of six), so the material is declared here for
//      the two that lack it. Without this line the M14's HUD icon would draw
//      "Could not load material" on Buried and Origins.
//
//  📝 fivesevendw_upgraded_zm's maxAmmo is the only other divergence (14 on
//  TranZit, 13 everywhere else); the def shipped is the 13 that five of the six
//  maps use. One reserve round on a dual-wield pistol, and it needs no asset.
// ============================================================================
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_raygun_view_upg
xmodel,t6_wpn_zmb_raygun_world_upg
material,hud_icon_m14

// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.1 - THE ONE ASSET CLASS THE v2.11.0 DIVERGENCE AUDIT ABOVE MISSED:
//  THE RUMBLE. A weapon def's fireRumble names a `rumble/<name>` RAWFILE, and a
//  missing rumble is NOT a soft "Could not load" like a model, a material or an
//  fx - it is a COM_ERROR that drops the whole map back to the menu:
//
//      Could not load rawfile "rumble/quadrotor_fly".
//      ====================== COM_ERROR (1) ===============
//      Could not load rumble info file file [rumble/quadrotor_fly]
//
//  That is the Origins boot of 2026-09-03 (console_zm.log 08:30, line 4831),
//  and it is v2.11.0's own doing: slowgun_upgraded_zm became a raw weapons\zm\
//  def in that build, so it now loads - and precaches - on all six maps, and
//  its fireRumble is `quadrotor_fly`, which Unlinker --list finds in exactly
//  ONE fastfile of the twenty-seven any map loads: zm_buried.ff.
//
//  🌟 The precedent was already in this tree and was simply not applied to the
//  new gun: mod.ff has shipped `heavygun_fire` for the Jet Gun (global since
//  v2.9.11) and `subwoofer_heavy` for the Thundergun for exactly this reason -
//  see mod_base.zone and mod_wonderweapons.zone. Three rawfiles, ~300 bytes.
//  Byte copies of zm_buried.ff's own, so the Paralyzer keeps Treyarch's exact
//  rumble on Buried and nothing changes anywhere else.
//
//  🛑 PRE-FLIGHT FOR ANY FUTURE RAW DEF (ERROR_CATALOGUE §53): before shipping
//  a weapons\zm\ def globally, read its fireRumble / meleeImpactRumble /
//  reloadRumble / explosionRumble and confirm each name is in a zone EVERY map
//  loads. All 87 raw defs were re-audited this way on 2026-09-03; quadrotor_fly
//  was the only miss, and the other three rumble fields are empty in all 87.
//
//  📝 The two `.rmb` payloads are named by the rumble file's own highRumbleFile
//  / lowRumbleFile fields, not by convention - subwoofer_heavy points at
//  tank_damage_heavy_{h,l}.rmb. quadrotor_fly points at its own name.
// ============================================================================
rawfile,rumble/quadrotor_fly
rawfile,rumble/quadrotor_fly_h.rmb
rawfile,rumble/quadrotor_fly_l.rmb

// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.4 - THE ELEVEN GUNS THE v2.11.0 RETARGET MISSED, found by auditing all
//  588 (map x upgraded weapon) pairs against per-zone Unlinker inventories.
//
//  SEVEN carry the mod's own "qol" variants and still named the STOCK camo asset
//  (camo_judge, camo_m16, camo_mp5, camo_olympia, camo_saiga, camo_saritch,
//  camo_x95l). Those names ARE defined by Green Run / Nuketown / Die Rise, whose
//  tables are 4 and 7 slots, so slot 8 - the animated camo, index 44 - does not
//  exist and the toggle drew nothing for them on those maps. The camo_qol_*
//  copies were already built and shipped in v2.11.0; only the defs were missed.
//  They are raw weapons\zm\ files, so no declaration is needed here.
//
//  FOUR more are the reverse case, and they are the ones declared below. On MOB
//  OF THE DEAD alone, ak47 / minigun_alcatraz / thompson / uzi resolve their
//  camo out of zm_prison.ff, whose copies have NO slot 3 (index 39, the camo
//  this mod uses when the animated toggle is OFF) - so those four packed to no
//  camo at all on Mob, while looking correct on all five other maps. Measured,
//  not inferred: zm_prison's camo_ak47 and camo_uzi are live at 36/37/40/44 and
//  camo_thompson / camo_minigun at 40/44 only.
//
//  🌟 NOTHING IS INVENTED HERE. mod.ff's OWN copies of all four are complete -
//  slots 3, 4, 8 and 12 all live - so camo_qol_<x> is a byte copy of mod.ff's
//  camo_<x>, and the four upgraded defs (zone_assets\weapons\) now name it. The
//  name exists in no retail fastfile, so mod.ff's copy is the only copy and the
//  §50 "the map's copy wins" ceiling cannot reach it. Off Mob this changes
//  nothing at all - those maps were already reading mod.ff's table.
//
//  The defs were diffed field by field: `camo` is the ONLY field that changed in
//  any of the eleven, and all seven raw files stay under the 20,480 B loader
//  ceiling (largest 20,384).
//
//  Only the four camo assets are declared below: the four weapon names are
//  already owned by mod.ff via mod_base.zone, and the Linker picks their edited
//  defs up from zone_assets\weapons\ on its own (ERROR_CATALOGUE 51) - declaring
//  them a second time here is a duplicate-asset error.
// ============================================================================
camo,camo_qol_ak47
camo,camo_qol_minigun
camo,camo_qol_thompson
camo,camo_qol_uzi

// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.5 - 🛑 THE REAL REASON THE ANIMATED CAMO WAS MISSING ON MOB, BURIED
//  AND ORIGINS: §50's ceiling applies to the MATERIAL as well as the camo asset.
//
//  MEASURED, from the user's own boot (console_zm.log 10:40, Mob of the Dead).
//  The probe added in v2.11.3 proved the script half was already perfect:
//      [zm_qol] camo: m1911_upgraded_zm startAmmo=56 -> mod.ff weapon defs live = 1
//      [zm_qol] papcamo: ak74u_extclip_upgraded_zm+reflex upgraded=1 camo_index=44 ...
//  Index 44 WAS applied, the camo table WAS mod.ff's, and its slot 8 WAS live -
//  and the gun still came out in a green-grey camo. Because slot 8 names the
//  MATERIAL mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2, and `Unlinker --list` finds that name
//  owned by zm_prison, zm_buried and zm_tomb (plus _1/_2/_3/_alt, and
//  zm_transit_patch owns _3). On those maps the MAP's copy wins, exactly as it
//  does for a camo asset - so the gun drew TREYARCH's DLC2 camo, not EZZ's.
//
//  Proof the two differ, dumped side by side from the shipped mod.ff and from
//  zm_prison.ff - same techniqueset, different textures:
//      mod.ff    Ember -> camo_stellar_ember   colorMap -> camo_goldgrid_nml
//      zm_prison Ember -> camo_zmb_dlc2_ember  colorMap -> ~-gcamo_zmb_dlc2_col
//  camo_stellar_ember decoded to PNG is the pink/purple nebula with stars. The
//  "broken green/white texture" the user reported is not broken at all - it is
//  Treyarch's own DLC2 camo, drawn because ours was shadowed.
//
//  🌟 THE FIX IS v2.11.0's OWN LESSON, ONE LEVEL FURTHER DOWN: give the thing a
//  name no retail map defines. mc/mtl_weapon_camo_qolanim* is a byte copy of the
//  EZZ-stamped dlc2 family under a name that exists in NO fastfile but this one,
//  and every camo table mod.ff owns now points its slot 8 at it. The original
//  mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2* assets stay OWNED and untouched - un-owning a name
//  something still references is the ERROR_CATALOGUE 35 crash class.
//
//  Seven more guns read a camo table the MAP owns on Mob / Buried / Origins, so
//  the table retarget could not reach them; their defs are mod-controlled, so
//  they now name a camo_qol_<x> copy instead (six mod.ff defs plus the raw
//  barretm82qol). Only `camo` changed in any of the seven.
// ============================================================================
//  Kept OWNED although nothing references it any more: the slot-8 rewrite above
//  took its last reference away and the Linker then dropped it, which is a -1 in
//  the asset delta and exactly the un-owning class of ERROR_CATALOGUE 35. Pinned
//  here so the delta stays +14 / -0.
material,mc/mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2_alt_3
camo,camo_qol_ballista
camo,camo_qol_ksg
camo,camo_qol_mp40
camo,camo_qol_scarh
camo,camo_qol_scorpionevo
camo,camo_qol_stg44

// ============================================================================
//  v2.11.6 - THE ANIMATED CAMO IS NOW THE DARK MATTER TEXTURE PACK, AND THE MOD
//  NO LONGER STAMPS ANYTHING ONTO A STOCK MATERIAL NAME.
//
//  What the user's boots proved, in order:
//    - v2.11.3's probe: the SCRIPT half was always right (index 44 applied, table
//      live, mod.ff defs live).
//    - v2.11.4 on Mob: the map's own mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2 drew Treyarch's DLC2
//      camo - the mod's EZZ-stamped copy was shadowed (ERROR_CATALOGUE 55).
//    - v2.11.5 on Mob: the un-shadowable copy (mtl_weapon_camo_qolanim) loaded
//      with no error and drew NOTHING. Its textures, camo_stellar_ember and
//      camo_goldgrid_nml, are 1440x1440 and 792x792 - not powers of two, unlike
//      every Treyarch camo texture (256/512) and the pack below (4096). That is
//      the one measurable difference between a material that draws and one that
//      does not, and it is why the EZZ camo was never seen anywhere.
//
//  So the whole material-stamping route (v2.9.26 EZZ, v2.11.5 qolanim) is gone:
//    - the 7 stamped mtl_weapon_camo_zmb_dlc2* materials are back to Treyarch's
//      exact contents (copied out of zm_prison.ff, textures and constants);
//      _alt_3 exists in no retail zone and stays as the donor shipped it.
//    - all 123 camo tables point slot 8 at those stock names again.
//    - the 8 qolanim materials and the 2 EZZ images are removed (nothing
//      references them any more - grep-verified before the relink).
//
//  THE ANIMATED LOOK IS NOW PURE PIXELS, the way every Plutonium texture pack
//  works. The 9 camo_zmb_dlc2* images stream from dlczm2/3/4.ipak on EVERY map,
//  indexed by R_HashString(name). 🛑 CORRECTED after the 11:58 boot: in
//  storage	6\images a loose file is read BY NAME, ipak-backed or not - the
//  user's own HD pack there is 980 by-name files, 329 of them DLC-ipak-only
//  (Origins' c_zom_mech_body1_n among them). The hash-name rule is mod.iwd's
//  (MOD_CATALOGUE 11a), and v2.11.6's first cut wrongly shipped the nine
//  hash-named; they are now by name. Both copies of the material - the map's on Mob /
//  Buried / Origins and mod.ff's elsewhere - name the same 9 images, so ONE set
//  of 9 by-name files reaches all six maps and the shadowing stops mattering.
//  The hash function is OpenAssetStudio's T6 R_HashString (djb2, xor, |0x20),
//  verified 32,212 / 32,212 against image_names.csv before use.
//
//  The same 9 files also sit by name in zone_assets\images (mod.ff's own headers,
//  4096x4096) and images\ (mod.iwd), so the mod's asset record matches the pack
//  on the three maps where mod.ff's image asset is the live one. Every file is
//  under the 16,777,280 B loose-image cap (ERROR_CATALOGUE, the HD pack case).
// ============================================================================
